import{_ as t,o as a,c as r,ak as o}from"./chunks/framework.B8jO0odJ.js";const u=JSON.parse('{"title":"GDD presentation illustrations","description":"Created October 8, 2026 for the illustrated, reader-facing GDD. All six PNGs are explanatory concepts, not game screenshots, production 3D models, verified phone layouts or ev","frontmatter":{"title":"GDD presentation illustrations","description":"Created October 8, 2026 for the illustrated, reader-facing GDD. All six PNGs are explanatory concepts, not game screenshots, production 3D models, verified phone layouts or ev","source":"docs/media/gdd/presentation/README.md","category":"Other documents","sourceUpdated":"2026-10-08T07:30:37+08:00","outline":[2,3]},"headers":[],"relativePath":"content/docs/media/gdd/presentation/readme.md","filePath":"content/docs/media/gdd/presentation/readme.md"}'),i={name:"content/docs/media/gdd/presentation/readme.md"};function n(s,e,l,d,c,h){return a(),r("div",null,[...e[0]||(e[0]=[o('<div><h1 id="gdd-presentation-illustrations">GDD presentation illustrations<a class="header-anchor" href="#gdd-presentation-illustrations" aria-label="Link to this section">​</a></h1><p>Created October 8, 2026 for the illustrated, reader-facing GDD. All six PNGs are explanatory concepts, not game screenshots, production 3D models, verified phone layouts or evidence of completed gameplay. The approved first two Chainy storyboards remain the visual source of truth. The third BlockForge storyboard remains gameplay context only.</p><h2 id="inventory">Inventory<a class="header-anchor" href="#inventory" aria-label="Link to this section">​</a></h2><table><thead><tr><th>File</th><th>Purpose</th><th>Dimensions</th><th>Method / editable source</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>world-map.png</td><td>Three equally accessible Web3, Blockchain and AI world concepts</td><td>1536 × 1024</td><td>Built-in image generation; prompt below</td></tr><tr><td>characters.png</td><td>Explorer, Blocky and Aira visual concept lineup</td><td>1536 × 1024</td><td>Built-in image generation; prompt below</td></tr><tr><td>lesson-storyboard.png</td><td>Four moments in a short guided lesson</td><td>1600 × 1000</td><td>Original SVG schematic: lesson-storyboard.svg</td></tr><tr><td>controls.png</td><td>Fixed activity view, reorder/check/reset controls</td><td>1600 × 1000</td><td>Original SVG schematic: controls.svg</td></tr><tr><td>mechanics.png</td><td>Bounded records, three copies, classifier and fixed-grid agent</td><td>1600 × 1050</td><td>Original SVG schematic: mechanics.svg</td></tr><tr><td>lesson-flow.png</td><td>Six-step learner journey</td><td>1600 × 950</td><td>Original SVG schematic: lesson-flow.svg</td></tr></tbody></table><p>The PNG illustrations accompany explanations in the main GDD/PDF. SVGs preserve editable labels and geometry. No source images were cropped, recolored, or otherwise modified to create these assets. The raster concepts were generated from descriptions of the approved style. Decorative slogans/extra scenery in world-map.png do not establish lesson content, game dialogue, assets or added world scope. The generated character proportions are a taller interpretation, not a newly approved character redesign. Use the original two approved references for final proportions. Character names and exact costume details remain concepts; the blue-haired yellow-coated explorer and friendly rounded robot identity derive from the approved references.</p><p>The control schematic depicts a worked ordering example. It omits secondary record details and linking dialogs for readability; it does not replace the complete mechanics specification. The replica panel uses a simplified classroom comparison rule under the stated lesson assumption, not secure real-world consensus. The agent grid agrees with the documented parcel/obstacle/destination fixture. The classifier panel shows training and separate test stages without claiming tested model delivery.</p><h2 id="production-and-checks">Production and checks<a class="header-anchor" href="#production-and-checks" aria-label="Link to this section">​</a></h2><ul><li>Built-in image generation was used for the two raster concepts; no API/CLI fallback was used.</li><li>Generated originals were copied into this project folder and preserved at the tool&#39;s original location.</li><li>Four original SVG diagrams were rendered with the workspace Sharp runtime.</li><li>All labels in the schematic SVGs are at least 32 pixels at 1600-pixel width. At 6.8-inch print width, 32 pixels is approximately 9.8 points; use the full content width.</li><li>Each generated image and each rendered diagram was visually reviewed. A crowded controls annotation was shortened and re-rendered.</li><li>These are document illustrations. Unity asset import, polygon/texture budgets, touch targets and device performance remain separate production checks. No untested runtime asset recommendation is implied.</li><li>Source provenance is recorded here; no rights to third-party reference art or a general legal clearance are asserted.</li></ul><h2 id="built-in-generation-prompts">Built-in generation prompts<a class="header-anchor" href="#built-in-generation-prompts" aria-label="Link to this section">​</a></h2><h3 id="world-map">World map<a class="header-anchor" href="#world-map" aria-label="Link to this section">​</a></h3><p>Use case: stylized-concept. Create a landscape 3:2 game design document concept illustration for CHAINY, an offline educational mobile game for ages 12–17. Toy-like polished rounded 3D diorama art, soft light, chunky geometry, readable shapes, blue-haired young explorer with yellow coat, yellow backpack and round golden hair/headphone discs standing small in foreground, friendly white robot with black face and cyan eyes. Main subject: THREE separate selectable floating islands arranged left-to-right, each a distinct world card: left Web3 teal/aqua village with linked community houses and a shield; middle Blockchain green-and-blue cubic landscape with three linked glowing record blocks; right AI violet city with a small friendly robot and abstract learning symbols. Clean sky-blue background, large islands with plenty of breathing room, all three worlds equally prominent, no route implying world prerequisites. Label each island with exact large readable words: &#39;WEB3&#39;, &#39;BLOCKCHAIN&#39;, &#39;AI&#39;. Top title &#39;CHOOSE A WORLD&#39;. Bottom subtitle &#39;Short lessons. Learn at your own pace.&#39; Restrained game UI framing, no coins, payments, leaderboard, lock symbols, joystick, extra worlds or implementation IDs. Characters must follow described blue hair/yellow explorer/white robot identity. All illustration is a proposed interface concept, not screenshot. High quality 3D animated-film-inspired material with matte plastic feel and soft shadows.</p><h3 id="characters">Characters<a class="header-anchor" href="#characters" aria-label="Link to this section">​</a></h3><p>Use case: stylized-concept. Create a landscape 3:2 character lineup for the CHAINY educational game design document. Three full-body figures in three equally spaced areas on a soft warm white/light blue studio background. Style: polished toy-like rounded 3D/chibi proportions, soft lighting, clean matte plastic and cloth materials, cheerful but respectful for teenage learners. Left &#39;EXPLORER&#39;: blue-haired character with short ponytail, yellow coat, yellow backpack, round golden hair/headphone discs, boots, friendly wave. Middle &#39;BLOCKY&#39;: friendly white and pale blue robot guide, square rounded head, black glass face, cyan glowing eyes, blue hexagonal emblem on chest, holding one translucent blue record block. Right &#39;AIRA&#39;: friendly white robot sharing the same rounded silhouette, violet shoulder accents, black glass face, cyan eyes, holding a small tablet displaying three simple colored example shapes. Text only the three exact names beneath corresponding figures. No weapons, coins, money, complex background, extra people, game UI, watermark, pose montage or turnarounds. Characters are concept illustrations for offline learning about Web3, blockchain and AI. Preserve coherent shared proportions and make hands and feet fully visible.</p></div>',1)])])}const m=t(i,[["render",n]]);export{u as __pageData,m as default};
